/**

@page page_exahype2_blockstructured Block-structured patch operations

\tableofcontents

ExaHyPE 2 embeds a patch into every cell of Peano's adaptive Cartesian grid. A
patch is a @f$ k \times k @f$ or @f$ k \times k \times k @f$ block of degrees of
freedom with an optional halo layer around it. The routines below operate on
that layout and are independent of the numerical scheme. The finite-volume, the
Runge-Kutta DG and the ADER-DG solvers assemble their kernels from them.

## Functionality

\li `exahype2/fv/FiniteVolumeScheme.h` Declares the finite-volume scheme on one
  patch. The class exahype2::fv::FiniteVolumeScheme writes the initial
  condition, fills the outer half of a boundary face, copies the boundary layers
  of a patch onto its faces, interpolates and restricts the halo halves across a
  level jump, interpolates and restricts a patch across a regrid and advances a
  patch by one time step. The free functions exahype2::fv::getFaceVolumeIndex()
  name the volumes of a face. The function exahype2::fv::getVolumeCentre()
  returns the centre of a volume. The header `exahype2/dg/Basis.h` derives the
  operators of the DG solver families from the quadrature nodes.
\li `exahype2/MultiresolutionDetail.h` Computes the relative representation
  error of an affine fit over one patch. The function exahype2::refineOnDetail()
  maps this error onto a refinement command.
\li `exahype2/Curvi.h` Maps a Cartesian domain onto a curvilinear domain with
  the same cell connectivity and back. The curvilinear cells need not be
  equidistant.

The class exahype2::plotter::PatchPlotter writes the patch data of a rank
through the file writer of the selected format in `tarch::plotter`.

*/
